===== The empirical null =====
Control genomes bred and selected alongside everything else: 306
Best train fitness reached by a CONTROL:  0.445   (control_random vt=0.10)
  that control's holdout min excess Sharpe: -0.124

  The survival threshold X = 0.000 IS PASSABLE BY LUCK at this population and
  generation count: coin-flip entries cleared it. Any survivor whose
  train fitness is at or below 0.445 is not distinguishable from noise,
  and is marked 'below null' above. Raise X, widen the environment set,
  or judge on the holdout columns only.

Real families whose train fitness beat the best control: 12/13
Non-control finalists with POSITIVE holdout excess Sharpe in EVERY environment: 11
Best non-control finalist by holdout: lppls_bubble+hawkes vt=0.20  (holdout min excess Sharpe 0.649)
  after correcting for 4294 candidates:
    Sharpe expected from luck alone (worst env): 2.079
    deflated Sharpe, worst environment:          0.036   <- NOT significant

===== Did selection transfer? =====
Rank correlation between what the search maximized (train fitness) and what
the holdout delivered, across the 21 tuned family champions.

  all families:        rho = 0.439, permutation p = 0.049   <- transfers
  better half only:    rho = 0.382, permutation p = 0.279   <- no evidence of transfer

  Read the second line, not the first. A search that only knows which ideas
  are hopeless will score well on the first line while being useless for the
  decision anybody actually makes, which is choosing among the good ones.

  On the holdout, the coin-flip control ranked 16 of 22 family champions.

